There are 2 types of access
	1. Console
	2. Remote

The console is a direct access to an operating system when it is connected through VGA, HDMI, DVI etc.

Remote access where we connect to os remotely over the network.
	- Windows to windows - RDP using Ip address
	
	- Macos to macos - sharing
	
	- Windows to linux - putty client using ip address
	For windows 10 or newer no need putty, SSH is built in
	Ø ssh ipaddress_of_linux

	- Linux to linux 
	Ø ssh ipaddress_of_linux
	
	Ø Ssh -l username ipaddress

